course: dictionary
lesson: 15841
title: Undisclosed: kept secret
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The start of a word often gives a clue. Un- means "not", and disclose means to make something known or to tell it. So undisclosed means not told and not made public.
explain: «The company paid an undisclosed sum to the team.» The news tells you a sum of money was paid, but it does not say how much. The word shows that the amount exists, but people were not told it.
explain: Check by swapping in a meaning. «The school kept the location of the trip undisclosed for safety reasons.» If you swap in "secret", you get "kept the location of the trip secret for safety reasons", which still makes sense, so undisclosed means secret.
fact: Undisclosed means not told or not made public; kept secret.
fact: «An undisclosed sum» means an amount of money that nobody has said.
fact: «An undisclosed location» means a place that is kept secret.
fact: «For undisclosed reasons» means someone chose not to say why.
fact: Undisclosed is mostly found in news and business writing, where it tells you that a fact exists but has not been shared.
exercise: «The company paid an undisclosed sum for the building.» What does undisclosed mean here? | The amount was paid in coins | The amount was very large | *The amount was kept secret | The building was empty
exercise: What does «an undisclosed location» mean? | A place that is far away | A place with no roads | A place full of water | *A place kept secret
exercise: The club gave no details and said it was for undisclosed reasons. What does this mean? | *The reasons were not told to people | The reasons were very funny | The reasons were written on a board | The reasons were all about food
test: «The school said the new head teacher's name would stay undisclosed until Monday.» What does undisclosed mean? | Known by everyone | Written in big letters | Shouted out loud | *Kept secret until it was told
test: Which word is the best swap for undisclosed in «an undisclosed sum»? | A broken amount | A happy amount | A large amount | *A secret amount
exam: Which word means not told or made public? | open | shouted | obvious | *undisclosed
